{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"WritingDirection","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Writing direction defines the base direction in which bidirectional text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"lays out its directional runs. A directional run is a contiguous sequence","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of characters that all have the same effective directionality, which can","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"be determined using the Unicode BiDi algorithm. The "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/AttributedString\/WritingDirection\/leftToRight","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"writing direction puts the directional run that is placed first in the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"storage leftmost, and places subsequent directional runs towards the","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"right. The "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/AttributedString\/WritingDirection\/rightToLeft","isActive":true},{"text":" writing direction puts the directional run","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that is placed first in the storage rightmost, and places subsequent","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"directional runs towards the left.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Note that writing direction is a property separate from a text’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"alignment, its line layout direction, or its character direction."},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"However, it is often used to determine the default alignment of a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"paragraph. E.g. English (a language with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/Locale\/LanguageDirection\/leftToRight","type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Locale\/Language-swift.struct\/characterDirection"},{"text":") is usually aligned","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to the left, but may be centered or aligned to the right for special","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"effect, or to be visually more appealing in a user interface.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"For bidirectional text to be perceived as laid out correctly, make sure","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that the writing direction is set to the value equivalent to the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Locale\/Language-swift.struct\/characterDirection"},{"text":" of the primary","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"language in the text. E.g. an English sentence that contains some","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Arabic (a language with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/Locale\/LanguageDirection\/rightToLeft","type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Locale\/Language-swift.struct\/characterDirection"},{"text":") words, should use","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/AttributedString\/WritingDirection\/leftToRight","type":"reference"},{"text":" writing direction. An Arabic sentence that contains","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"some English words, should use a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/AttributedString\/WritingDirection\/rightToLeft","type":"reference"},{"text":" writing direction.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Writing direction is always orthogonoal to the line layout direction","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"chosen to display a certain text. The line layout direction is the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"direction in which a sequence of lines is placed in. E.g. English text","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is usually displayed with a line layout direction of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/Locale\/LanguageDirection\/topToBottom","type":"reference"},{"text":". While languages do","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"have an associated line language direction (see","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Locale\/Language-swift.struct\/lineLayoutDirection"},{"text":"), not all displays","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of text follow the line layout direction of the text’s primary language.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Horizontal script is script with a line layout direction of either","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/Locale\/LanguageDirection\/topToBottom","type":"reference"},{"text":" or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/Locale\/LanguageDirection\/bottomToTop","type":"reference"},{"text":". Vertical script","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"has a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/Locale\/LanguageDirection\/leftToRight","type":"reference"},{"text":" or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/Locale\/LanguageDirection\/rightToLeft","type":"reference"},{"text":" line layout","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"direction. In vertical scripts, a writing direction of ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/AttributedString\/WritingDirection\/leftToRight","type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is interpreted as top-to-bottom and a writing direction of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/AttributedString\/WritingDirection\/rightToLeft","type":"reference"},{"text":" is interpreted as bottom-to-top.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"FoundationEssentials"}],"fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"WritingDirection","kind":"identifier"}],"symbolKind":"enum","roleHeading":"Enumeration","platforms":[{"name":"iOS","introducedAt":"26.0","deprecated":false,"unavailable":false,"beta":false},{"name":"iPadOS","introducedAt":"26.0","deprecated":false,"unavailable":false,"beta":false},{"name":"Mac Catalyst","introducedAt":"26.0","deprecated":false,"unavailable":false,"beta":false},{"name":"macOS","introducedAt":"26.0","deprecated":false,"unavailable":false,"beta":false},{"name":"tvOS","introducedAt":"26.0","deprecated":false,"unavailable":false,"beta":false},{"name":"visionOS","introducedAt":"26.0","deprecated":false,"unavailable":false,"beta":false},{"name":"watchOS","introducedAt":"26.0","deprecated":false,"unavail